---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { paths, site } from '../data/site';

const lang = 'en';
const t = site[lang];
const d = t.downloads;
const releaseUrl = 'https://github.com/MXGG/myair-site/releases';

const capabilityGroups = [
	['Core workflow', ['Level-2 product loading', 'Low-degree replacement and anomaly baseline', 'Filter route management', 'Grid synthesis and export']],
	['Analysis tools', ['Basin average extraction', 'Annual and semi-annual amplitude fitting', 'Trend estimation', 'Regional correction workflow']],
	['Quality review', ['Global map preview', 'Residual stripe inspection', 'Reference product comparison', 'Processing log export']],
];

const releaseRows = [
	['V01', 'Windows installer', 'Published through Releases', 'Desktop package for GRACE Level-2 processing, filtering, preview, and basin analysis.'],
	['Portable archive', 'Optional package', 'Use when available', 'No-install archive for testing or classroom demonstration when an installer is not preferred.'],
	['Example configuration', 'Small config files', 'Stored with documentation', 'Configuration templates for GSM input, filter routing, grid synthesis, and export rules.'],
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang={t.langCode}>
<head><BaseHead title={`${d.title} | ${t.title}`} description={d.lead} lang={lang} alternateHref={paths.zh.downloads} /></head>
<body>
<Header lang={lang} alternateHref={paths.zh.downloads} />
<main class="page-shell downloads-shell">
	<section class="page-hero compact downloads-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Software</p><h1>GRACE Level-2 Processing Software</h1><p>The software page introduces the desktop workflow and release package for GRACE/GRACE-FO Level-2 data preparation, filtering experiments, EWH synthesis, basin analysis, and preview quality control.</p></section>
	<section class="software-card" aria-labelledby="software-title"><div class="software-main"><p class="section-label">Release package</p><h2 id="software-title">Installer and versioned package</h2><p>The package is intended for local GRACE Level-2 processing practice. It organizes source products, correction settings, filter routes, visualization previews, and export metadata in one reproducible workflow.</p><div class="software-actions"><a class="button primary" href={releaseUrl}>{d.button}</a><span>{d.releaseHint}</span></div></div><div class="software-meta" aria-label="Software metadata">{d.meta.map(([key, value]) => <div><span>{key}</span><strong>{value}</strong></div>)}</div></section>
	<section class="software-overview" aria-labelledby="software-overview-title"><div class="section-heading wide-heading"><p class="section-label">OVERVIEW</p><h2 id="software-overview-title">Capability map</h2><p>The capability map describes the actual scope of the GRACE Level-2 visualization and processing software.</p></div><div class="capability-column-grid">{capabilityGroups.map(([title, items]) => <article class="capability-column"><h3>{title}</h3><ul>{items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div></section>
	<section class="release-table-card" aria-labelledby="release-table-title"><h2 id="release-table-title">Release information</h2><div class="responsive-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Type</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{releaseRows.map((row) => <tr>{row.map((cell) => <td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
	<section class="download-feature-grid" aria-label="Software features">{d.features.map((feature) => <article class="download-feature-card"><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.text}</p></article>)}</section>
	<section class="faq-card" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2><details><summary>What should I check before installing?</summary><p>Confirm the release version, supported Windows version, package type, and whether the example configuration matches your GRACE product layout.</p></details><details><summary>Where are software packages hosted?</summary><p>The download button points to the GitHub Releases page, where packages and release notes should be collected in one versioned location.</p></details></section>
</main>
<Footer lang={lang} />
</body>
</html>
